      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "So in the previous lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "you learned how you can deploy an Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.25,
          "en": "as a single page application to Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.25,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "And of course, Firebase hosting was just one example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "Of course, you can deploy Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "to any host as mentioned in the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "Now, it's also worth noting that in that last lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "I showed you the manual deployment approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "which is good to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 36.867,
          "en": "But it turns out that you can actually also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.867,
          "end": 40.323,
          "en": "the Angular CLI for deployment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.52,
          "end": 45.84,
          "en": "because the Angular CLI gives you a command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.84,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "the ng add command, which you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "to add third-party libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "that support this command to Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 61.52,
          "en": "And this command will then not just install those libraries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "you could do that with npm install,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "but it will also configure them for your Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "or configure your project for those libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 75.72,
          "en": "depending on how you wanna look at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.72,
          "end": 80.72,
          "en": "And there, for example, is an @angular/fire library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "which you can add with that ng add command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "which will in the end add Firebase to your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "which will enable Firebase hosting in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "And the CLI will then also give you an ng deploy command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 100.86,
          "en": "which will in the end, build the application for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 103.28999999999999,
          "en": "and then deploy the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103.28999999999999,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "to that configured deployment provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 108.87299999999999,
          "en": "so to Firebase, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "And that would've been an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "And I'm also mentioning this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "because there also are other deployment providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.66,
